[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Scalable Jenkins CI/CD with Kubernetes Cloud Plugin and Dynamic Pod Agents"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Traditional Jenkins architectures rely on static build agents that remain online continuously, leading to resource wastage and maintenance overhead. By integrating the Jenkins Kubernetes Cloud Plugin, you can spin up dynamic, ephemeral build agents inside a Kubernetes cluster on-demand. This tutorial guides you through configuring the Kubernetes plugin to provision pods dynamically for each pipeline execution and terminate them immediately afterward."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Architecture Overview"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"A running Kubernetes cluster (v1.22+ recommended)."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"A functioning Jenkins instance deployed either inside or outside the cluster."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Cluster admin permissions to create ServiceAccounts, Roles, and RoleBindings."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 1: Configuring Kubernetes RBAC for Jenkins"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"To allow the Jenkins controller to create and manage pods within your Kubernetes cluster, you must set up appropriate Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Create a dedicated namespace and service account."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"kubectl create namespace jenkins
kubectl create serviceaccount jenkins-sa -n jenkins
kubectl create clusterrolebinding jenkins-cluster-rule --clusterrole=cluster-admin --serviceaccount=jenkins:jenkins-sa"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 2: Installing the Kubernetes Plugin"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Navigate to your Jenkins dashboard, go to Manage Jenkins > Plugins > Available plugins, and search for 'Kubernetes'. Install the plugin and restart your Jenkins instance if prompted."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 3: Configuring the Cloud Connection"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once installed, configure the Kubernetes cloud provider in Jenkins: Go to Manage Jenkins > Clouds > New Cloud > Kubernetes. Provide your Kubernetes URL (e.g., https://kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local if Jenkins runs inside the cluster) and select the appropriate Kubernetes Service Account credential."},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 4: Defining Dynamic Pod Templates"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Pod templates define the structure of the dynamic agents. While you can configure these via the UI, defining them declaratively within your Jenkinsfile is the modern, flexible approach. Below is an example of a declarative pipeline utilizing a dynamic pod with Maven and Docker containers."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"pipeline {
    agent {
        kubernetes {
            yaml '''
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  namespace: jenkins
  labels:
    some-label: jenkins-agent
spec:
  containers:
  - name: maven
    image: maven:3.8.6-openjdk-11
    command: ['cat']
    tty: true
  - name: docker
    image: docker:git
    command: ['cat']
    tty: true
    volumeMounts:
    - mountPath: /var/run/docker.sock
      name: docker-sock
  volumes:
  - name: docker-sock
    hostPath:
      path: /var/run/docker.sock
'''
        }
    }
    stages {
        stage('Build with Maven') {
            steps {
                container('maven') {
                    sh 'mvn --version'
                }
            }
        }
        stage('Docker Build') {
            steps {
                container('docker') {
                    sh 'docker version'
                }
            }
        }
    }
}"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 5: Verification and Cleanup"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Trigger a build for the pipeline defined above. While the build runs, open a terminal and execute 'kubectl get pods -n jenkins'. You will observe a dynamic pod spinning up with a randomized hash suffix. Once the pipeline completes successfully or fails, the pod terminates automatically, ensuring zero resource leakage."}]
